{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1521310-alternate-allegiances","id":1521310,"title":"Alternate Allegiances","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-23T21:01:32-07:00","id":1521310,"title":"Alternate Allegiances","content":"This is mostly just some brainstorming on my part. I haven't read the full write ups for the various allegiances in TC: Adventure!, and the original version only had a paltry four of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I am a long time fan of Pulp Adventure from as far back as seeing <i>Raiders of the Lost Ark</i> as a kid in 1982, as well as a history nerd. So I just felt like making a bunch of alternate groups for PCs to work for (or against in some cases). <br /> This is very much a work in progress, and a few of the names are sort of place holders. Also no abilities or other character creation mechanics usually associated with allegiances, at least not yet. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Heroes of Light</b><br /> <br /> These groups are your basic straightforward hero types. Morally upright men and women of derring do who fight evil with their wits, inventions, and punch to the jaw. <br /> <br /> <b>The Aeon Society for Gentlemen (and Ladies)</b><br /> You know who they are. Maxwell Mercer and his merry band of adventurers. They have meeting places in Chicago, New York, London, Alexandria, Bombay, Hong Kong, Sydney, Buenos Aires, and San Fransisco. The original group are spread across the world, each pursuing their own projects, leaving much of the Society's everyday mission to be done by groups of younger adventurers (ie the PCs). <br /> <br /> <b>The Knights of the Sky</b><br /> Fearless aviators from all over the world, originally made up of Great War veterans and augmented by barnstorming daredevils and aviation pioneers. This includes scientists and engineers working on ideas for jet engine technology. They see themselves as modern day knights errant who travel wherever needed to battle villains and help the helpless. It is rumored that Howard Hughes is a financial patron of the group. <br /> The Knights are meant to evoke classic pulp heroes such as G-8 and his Battle Aces, Biggles, Connie Kurridge, Captain Midnight, and Commando Cody, as well as more modern ones like the Rocketeer and Sky Captain. <br /> <br /> <b>The International Detective Agency</b><br /> A private investigative agency who operate around the world. Founded before the turn of the century, they strive to recruit the best investigative minds who will uphold the Agency's code of morals and ethics. In contrast to their rivals, the Pinkerton Agency, they refuse to work as hired muscle or enforcers. <br /> The Agency are meant to provide resources for characters in the style of classic detectives such as Dick Tracy, Hercule Poirot, Sam Spade, Nero Wolf, Nick &amp; Nora Charles, Kogoro Akechi, Huo Sang, Bulldog Drummond, Parashor Barma, Byomkesh Bakshi, Charlie Chan, Napoleon Bonaparte*, Tommy &amp; Tuppence, and Nancy Drew, among countless others. <br /> *(Not the French Emperor, but a mixed race Australian Aborigine police inspector introduced in 1929.) <br /> <br /> <b>The Order of Tomorrow</b><br /> A collective of scientists, inventors, and futurists who believe in a brighter and better tomorrow through the power of technology and idealism. Their focus is on the empowerment of the individual, and as such have always welcomed members of any gender, race, creed, or nationality, as long as they share these ideals. <br /> The Order is meant to highlight the positive aspects of modern science and pulp super science. They are heroes in the style of Doc Savage and his men (and his cousin, Pat Savage), Carson Napier, Tom Swift, Captain Future, Captain Hazzard, and Professor Calculus, as well as more modern characters like Tom Strong and Atomic Robo.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mapmakers</b><br /> Explorers who brave the great unknown, both because it's there and to protect it from those who might exploit or ruin it. Existing since since at least the 18th century, they understand that the world is full of strangeness and wonder, and wish to keep it that way. They are as much archaeologists and and scientists as they are retired hunters and native heroes. <br /> The Mapmakers are meant to evoke the adventurers who travel to the wild and &quot;uncivilized&quot; corners of the world or who call such places their home. Such classic heroes as Professor Challenger, Tintin, El Borak, Tarzan and Jane Porter, Fau-Tan, Fantomah, John Carter, Flash Gordon, and Popeye, as well as modern characters like Indiana Jones.<br /> <br /> <b>The Temple of Light</b><br /> A mystical order dedicated to protecting the world from arcane evil. Its members often develop and cultivate uncanny powers of the mind and a knowledge of occult rituals. These are heroes in the vein of Carnacki, Mandrake the Magician, the Green Lama, Doctor Occult, Jules de Grandin, Simon Iff, and Diana Marburg, as well as more modern ones such as Trevor Bruttenholm from Hellboy. <br /> <br /> <br /> Next, part 2, Agents of Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T21:18:01-07:00","id":1521312,"title":"","content":"My only nitpick is that yours groups are de facto rebranded official Allegiances of era. <br /> <br /> <b>Knights of the Sky</b> = official <b>Air Circus</b> with Knights errands ethos<br /> <br /> <b>Heroes of the Light + Mapmakers </b>= official <b>Aeon Society</b><br /> <br /> Only <b>Order of Tommorow</b> and <b>Temple of Light</b> are truy new. <br /> <br /> <b>Order of Tommorow</b> can be 'good part' of future <b>Transtendent Alliance </b>( From TC Core) - where <b>Rational Experimentation Group</b> ( From Adventure Jumpstart ) would clearly be 'Nazi scientists' organization. <br /> <br /> <b>Temple of Ligh</b>t is truly new, as Adventure wanted to deemphazise magic and Occult in the setting. I like your idea better. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T21:30:42-07:00","id":1521313,"title":"","content":"&quot;Heroes of Light&quot; isn't a group. It's an umbrella descriptor for the six organizations. (The same way &quot;Agents of Twilight&quot; is for the next batch.) <br /> <br /> The Mapmakers are just a precursor of the Global Cartography Initiative, as well as a revision of the Ponatowski Foundation with all the Czar baggage removed. <br /> <br /> And I just never really cared much for the Air Circus name. I think of the Knights as a possible evolution of the group in the ten years since the original game's setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T22:31:05-07:00","id":1521315,"title":"","content":"<b>Part 2: Agents of Twilight</b><br /> <br /> Not all heroes are shining paragons of society. Some operate in a grey area of legality, pursing their ideas of justice even when it puts them against the powers that be. <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Department 13&quot;</b><br /> They don't have a public name, at least not one they share. In truth, they are made up of a number of international government organizations. America's Branch 9, Britain's Unicorn Chamber, and France's Cabinet d'Curiosit\u00e9s are just some of them. Each is tasked with protecting its nation and the world from the dangers of unexplained phenomena, as well as trying to harness them for government use. This second objective will sometimes place them at odds with more open organizations. <br /> These are the characters similar to Operator 5, Secret Agent X-9, the FBI agents at the end of &quot;The Shadows Over Innsmouth&quot;, and Hellboy's BPRD. <br /> <br /> <b>The Scales of Justice</b><br /> The hard times of the Great Depression call for hard justice. A loose alliance of masked vigilantes who battle criminals above the law, often in a lethal fashion. <br /> Made for characters inspired by The Shadow, The Spider, The Green Hornet, The Phantom, the Bat, the Golden Bat, Miss Fury, and The Avenger. <br /> <br /> <b>L'Fant\u00f4mes</b><br /> The society of gentleman thieves from the Trinity Continuum core book. <br /> Besides the obvious characters such as Ars\u00e8ne Lupin, The Saint, and Cing\u00f6z Recai, it's also the place for the likes of the Domino Lady, the Crimson Clown, and the Fiend with Twenty Faces.<br /> <br /> <b>The Red Brigade</b><br /> Power to the People. The Brigade are collective of revolutionary cells and cadres scattered across the globe. They fight for the Proletariat, working for the eventual overthrow of Capitalism and the establishment of a Socialist (or Communist or Anarchist or ...) utopia. A large number of the Brigade are well meaning idealists and those fighting for socio-economic justice. Unfortunately, the entire upper echelons are entirely made up of loyal agents of the murderous totalitarian Soviet regime in Moscow. It is possible that some faction within the Brigade (ie the PCs) might manage to free the group from Stalin's grip. <br /> There isn't really any well known period examples for this, save maybe Tom Joad. But reading George Orwell's <i>Down and Out in Paris and London</i> and <i>Homage to Catalonia</i> may be useful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Next, part 3, Forces of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T15:18:53-07:00","id":1521409,"title":"","content":"<b>Forces of Darkness</b><br /> <br /> Bad guys and villains. While traditional Pulp tends to have a pretty black &amp; white morality, more modern interpretations may allow for a bit of leeway. In addition, it's always possible to have more heroic groups have to work with their more reasonable enemies against a common, worse threat. And a member of a villainous organization can always reform and end up one of the heroes. <br /> <br /> <b>The World Crime League</b><br /> The masters of the underworld. An alliance of several major criminal organizations, including ones from China, Europe, North America, and the Middle East. <br /> <br /> <b>The Futurist </b><b>Alliance</b><br /> The dark counterpart to the Order of Tomorrow, advancing the belief in a future world order run by experts and enlightened elites. Their agenda includes promotion of eugenics, Fascism, corporate monopolies, population control, and command economies, among other items. <br /> <br /> <b>The Invictus</b><br /> War is Man's natural state, separating the weak from the strong, and the Strong have the right to conquer and rule over the weak. The wave of anti-war sentiment which followed the Great War was anathema to the group's founders. They are now a private army out to create their own global empire, at the expense of both existing powers no longer willing or able to defend their possessions and the few unclaimed or undiscovered lands (including places like the Hollow Earth). <br /> <br /> <b>The Black Sun</b><br /> A mysterious organization - almost a cult - which delves into the strange new sciences and events of the new age. They possess their own strange - some would say alien - sciences, as well as abilities that border on the mystical. <br /> <br /> <b>The Cult of the Elder Gods</b><br /> A secretive cult devoted to alien and inhuman beings they claim dwell beyond the stars and secretly guide the human race. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T00:12:31-07:00","id":1521421,"title":"","content":"A few others I am poking around at is a global news organization for journalist characters like Tintin, Brenda Starr and Lois Lane, and Baron Saturday's organization as a group whose status depends on which perspective you are looking at them from. And some sort of Chinese organization that mixes Pulp with Wuxia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}